title: Roguelike turns
intro: Grid movers that take turns, with no code: everything moves when the player moves.
project: Empty | Crawl

chapter: A dungeon | A grid player and two grid enemies
create: Tilemap
rename: Level
set: Tilemap.Tiles = 11111111111111\n1............1\n1............1\n1.....11.....1\n1............1\n1............1\n11111111111111
select: Main Camera
set: Transform.Position.X = 7
set: Transform.Position.Y = -3.5
look: 7, -3.5, 4.5
deselect
create: Grid Player
set: Transform.Position.X = 2.5
set: Transform.Position.Y = -2.5
add: Health
deselect
create: Grid Enemy
rename: Slime
set: Transform.Position.X = 11.5
set: Transform.Position.Y = -2.5
set: GridChase.Range = 0
deselect
create: Grid Enemy
rename: Bat
set: Transform.Position.X = 11.5
set: Transform.Position.Y = -4.5
set: GridChase.Range = 3
say: Here's a small dungeon with a grid player, a slime that comes after the player from anywhere, and a bat that only notices it close up.

chapter: Taking turns | Entity, Gameplay, Turn Order
deselect
create: Turn Order
explain: menu:Entity | Entity, Gameplay, Turn Order | Turn Order makes the game turn-based. In a scene with grid movers, it sets up a roguelike.
explain: field:TurnOrder.Between | Between | Turns follow straight on, with no gap between them, and its text counts the turns.
select: Player
explain: component:TurnTaker | Turn Taker | Every grid mover got a Turn Taker. The player is on the Player team.
explain: field:TurnTaker.Actions | Actions | With one action, each step the player takes is their whole turn.
select: Slime
explain: component:TurnTaker | Enemy team | The slime and the bat are on the Enemy team, also with one action each: one step, or one swing, a turn.

chapter: Everything moves when you move | Step, and the dungeon answers
play
wait: 1
expectat: Slime = 11.5, -2.5
explain: game | Waiting on you | Nothing moves until the player does.
tap: Right
wait: 0.6
expectat: Player = 3.5, -2.5
expectat: Slime = 10.5, -2.5
explain: game | One step each | The player steps, and the slime steps once after them. The bat is too far away to notice, so it passes rather than holding up the turn.
tap: Right
wait: 0.6
tap: Right
wait: 0.6
tap: Right
wait: 0.6
expectat: Slime = 7.5, -2.5
expectat: Bat = 11.5, -4.5
say: Step by step, the slime closes in.
tap: Tab
wait: 1.2
expectvalue: Player.Health.Current = 2
expectvalue: Turns.TurnOrder.Round = 6
explain: game | A swing for a turn | Tab waits a turn. Next to the player, the slime swings instead of stepping, and its blow lands before the player can move again.
stop
say: That's roguelike turns with no code. Grid patrols wait whole turns at their points, and in network games each player's steps count on the host.
